{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on 11210895 for the cutover head (05d618e2). Questions 1\nto 3 have their rulings in 080e7c84, filed at 16:34.\n\n4. The `notice-source` rule records { scope, genesis, seq, hash }.\nDo not keep `inc`. The slot type and the inbox definition data\nchange with it, and the new pins belong to the cutover family\n(9ecd3efa). No definition of that family records an incarnation.\nIf another platform rule or slot still records `inc`, change it in\nthe same way and list it in the review request.\n\n5. A hand-written genesis is acceptable for a scripted test peer.\nThree conditions hold. One helper, `scriptedSequence`, makes every\nsuch genesis. The scripted resolver admits its bytes through the\nreal `admitSequenceGenesis`, with no test-only constructor and no\nskipped check. A test that claims something about the peer's own\njudged entries uses `ledgerSource`. A test whose subject is the\nreceiver uses the scripted peer. Do not move the existing sites to\na real ledger.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}